+# Trajectory observations in contribution envelopes
+
+Trajectory-v1 `observation` records describe environment output. The parser
+preserves their text and marks them with `record_type=trajectory_observation`.
+Envelope conversion carries these records as `Feedback`, with the marker intact,
+through the ordinary content redactor. It does not assign a tool identity,
+tool-call result, user rating or physical-success outcome.
+
+System records and unrelated opaque records retain their content exclusion.
+An observation is not trusted proof that an action succeeded. Consumers must
+interpret the provenance marker rather than treating every Feedback event as a
+user evaluation. This is an additive projection onto the existing v1 event enum;
+no server route, consent scope, reward rule or protocol enum is introduced.
+
+Regression coverage runs an ordinary trajectory through parsing, envelope
+conversion and deterministic local redaction, checks the marker and missing tool
+identity, and verifies that system and unrecognized opaque text remain excluded.
